Let $\begin{aligned}
K_f &:= \mathrm{functional\ knowledge},\\
K_r &:= \mathrm{knowledge\ in\ relationship}.\end{aligned}$ Then the spoken distinction is: $K_f \neq K_r.$ Functional knowledge belongs to practical operation. Knowledge in relationship is knowledge as image, memory, tradition, past experience, and observer. It is the accumulated picture of another human being.

