p.src:
Krishnamurti then links freedom to order: $\mathrm{Freedom}
\longrightarrow
\mathrm{Order}.$ And he adds: $\mathrm{Order}=\mathrm{Virtue}.$ Anderson helps unfold the word virtue. Virtue is not merely conformity to a rule. It is the ability to act. But if what we call action is only reaction, then it is repetition: $\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Reaction} &= \mathrm{Repetition},\\
\mathrm{Action} &\neq \mathrm{Reaction}.\end{aligned}$ Action, in this strict sense, is creative action. It is not the modified repetition of the past.

