p.src:
At this point Krishnamurti turns to listening. The difficulty, he says, is that most people do not listen. If they do listen, they listen through conclusions. A communist listens up to a point; a mind already translating what it hears hears only its own distortion. Listening through conclusions is another continuation of the known: $\mathrm{Listening\ through\ Conclusions}
\longrightarrow
\mathrm{Continuation\ of\ the\ Known}.$ By contrast: $\mathrm{Listening\ itself}
\longrightarrow
\mathrm{Attention}.$

