p.src:
The lecture closes by returning to relationship. When there is conflict in relationship, society furthers that conflict through education, national sovereignty, ideology, and the ordinary machinery of collective life. The serious question is therefore not abstract: $\mathrm{Relationship}
+
\mathrm{Freedom}
+
\mathrm{Knowledge}.$ These are not three separate topics. The question is whether functional knowledge can operate without becoming the observer in relationship, and whether relationship can be free of division.

